{"v":1,"accession":"PRJEB14602","title":"The oral and skin microbiomes of captive Komodo Dragons are significantly shared with their habitat.","description":"Here we collect saliva, skin, and fecal samples from captive Komodo dragons (V. komodoensis) and other captive varanids (V. olivaceus, V. indicus, V. rudicollis) in the first-ever culture-independent assessment of the varanid microbiome. Environmental samples were also collected to characterize host-environment microbiome sharing. This study adds crucial information to our understanding of captive Komodo dragon microbial ecology.","center":"University of California San Diego Microbiome Initiative","data_type":"Other","submission_date":"2016/06/28 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMEA4051333","1747.200197.holding.pen2.dirt.plant.matter; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)","uncertain",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMEA4051334","1747.200197.holding.pen2.straw; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)","uncertain",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMEA4051346","1747.209107.holding.pen.A.debris; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)","uncertain",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMEA4051349","1747.212070.holding.pen.B.debris; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)",